PhoneWindowManager: Let holding the power button turn the screen on and off

The Echo Shows' power button is also their privacy button. Their privacy
chips act on it whatever Android does.

The Echo Show 5's chip turns privacy on and off on any press shorter than
about 3 seconds and leaves it alone on a longer one. A short press to turn
the screen off or on therefore also turned privacy on or off.
LONG_PRESS_POWER_TOGGLE_SCREEN (7), set through power_button_long_press,
turns the screen off or back on once the button has been held for
ro.config.long_press_power_screen_ms, 3200 by default, past the chip's
threshold. A press on a sleeping screen waits for it instead of waking the
screen at once. Android does nothing on a short press, so the short press
only does what the chip does.

The Echo Show 8's chip does the opposite. A hold of about a second and a
half turns privacy on and off at its release. Any press turns it off.
Android took a hold for a short press at its release, so the screen went
off with it. LONG_PRESS_POWER_PRIVACY_HOLD (8) turns the screen off or back
on with a press released before ro.config.power_privacy_hold_ms, 500 by
default. It does nothing on a longer one. A press on a sleeping screen
waits for the release. While the file named by ro.config.power_privacy_state
reads 1, Android leaves the press to the chip.

